CON-07: subtract only pervious-surface evaporation from the GW ET budget

getSubareaRunoff() is called for IMPERV0, IMPERV1 and PERV in that order and
added the running total Vevap to Vpevap at the pervious call, so Vpevap held
the evaporation of all three subareas. gwater_getGroundwater() subtracts it
from the evaporation available to the aquifer, so water evaporating from the
impervious surface took ET away from the soil and the saturated zone.
Vol I eq. 5-11/5-12 subtract only the pervious surface's evaporation, as 5.1
did before 5.1.008 and as lid.c still does for LID units. Add only the
pervious subarea's own evaporation.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-07_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/subcatch.c b/src/legacy/engine/subcatch.c
index 7c1d97c..ed949fc 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/subcatch.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/subcatch.c
@@ -981,7 +981,7 @@ double getSubareaRunoff(int j, int i, double area, double precip, double evap,
     // --- update total inflow, evaporation & infiltration volumes
     Vinflow += precip * area * tStep;
     Vevap += surfEvap * area * tStep;
-    if ( i == PERV ) Vpevap += Vevap;
+    if ( i == PERV ) Vpevap += surfEvap * area * tStep;
     Vinfil += infil * area * tStep;
 
     // --- assign adjusted runoff coeff. & storage to shared variables
